(global_label "COIL_RAIL_OK" (shape passive) (at 359.41 226.06 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "7c5ddcfd-1bcd-4a03-b0e2-c85aad860411"))
(text "Heartbeat: Nexperia tW = K * REXT(kOhm) * CEXT(pF) ns, K about 1 above 10 nF. 100k and 3.3 uF is 330 ms typical. C50 is a 50 V X7R in 1206 so 3.3 V bias does not collapse that pulse. Measure it on the first board.\\nLong case, K=1.2 and capacitor +20 percent, is about 475 ms. A static level does not retrigger.\\nThe prototype firmware does not edge GPIO1, so Q stays low and both coils stay off. Do not modify that firmware.\\nQ_UP, Q_DN and Q_SERIES are ZXMS6004FF. R60 and R70 are 1k so the input stays above the 3.0 V on-threshold at 100 uA. Each input has a 100k pulldown. The other request clamps that input off.\\nBoth requests high: both inputs are clamped off. One request, fresh heartbeat: that coil pulls in.\\nNo part on this board joins COM to NO. A diode across each contactor coil is an installation part, at the contactor. A shorted diode there cannot hold the contactor on.\\nContact copper is 1.2 mm. IPC-2221 external 1 oz, 10 C, is about 1.07 mm at 2.5 A, which is Quick's recommended control fuse for a T6315-12 or T6415-12." (at 250 140 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))) (uuid "8e2da029-711c-4a56-a4e0-1f81242a79c3"))
  (embedded_fonts no)
)
